          %h2#references References
          %p
            The terminology of the flat-modality in the above sense was introduced – in the language of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-toposes
            and as part of the axioms on “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"}>
              cohesive
              = succeed "-toposes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            ” – in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
